## Aim
To analyze property data using Pandas and determine average listing prices by location, count properties with more than four bedrooms, and find the property with the largest area.

## Algorithm
1. Start the program.
2. Import the Pandas library.
3. Create a DataFrame containing property details.
4. Group properties by location and calculate the average price.
5. Count properties with more than four bedrooms.
6. Find the property with the largest area.
7. Display all results.
8. Stop the program.

## Code

```python
import pandas as pd

property_data = {
    "Property_ID": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5],
    "Location": ["Chennai", "Nellore", "Chennai",
                 "Hyderabad", "Nellore"],
    "Bedrooms": [3, 5, 4, 6, 2],
    "Area": [1200, 1800, 1500, 2500, 1000],
    "Price": [5000000, 7000000, 6000000,
              9000000, 4000000]
}

df = pd.DataFrame(property_data)

print("Average Price by Location:")
print(df.groupby("Location")["Price"].mean())

print("\\nProperties with More Than 4 Bedrooms:")
print(len(df[df["Bedrooms"] > 4]))

print("\\nProperty with Largest Area:")
print(df.loc[df["Area"].idxmax()])
```

## Input
Property details are provided in the DataFrame.

